{%- comment -%}
  The page's card groups (content model part 4, P-16): its own grids of cards, such as the three
  organisations on About or the ways to give on Donate. Staff add card groups to the page's Card
  groups field; this section shows them in order after the page text. A page without card groups
  shows nothing here.

  A group whose cards all have portrait images (a board, a staff list) shows as a grid of people:
  portrait frames, two to four across, smaller titles (DS-37). Staff don't choose it; the images do.
  A card that opens a PDF is a document, never a person, whatever its cover's shape (DS-69).
  A group of four or eight people goes two, then four across, as cards do (DS-44).

  Proposed (DS-73 to DS-76), each decided by the cards, never a setting:
  - A group whose cards all open a PDF is a shelf of documents: document tiles (gs-doc-tile) in a
    grid of artworks, two then three across, each cover whole on the mat and the title in the label
    style, as an artist's documents are (DS-108, which replaces DS-75's shelf).
  - A group whose cards all have a picture and their own action label ("Reserve a Clay Kit") is a
    list of offers: one per row, picture beside text from 750 px, as events are (DS-76).
  - A group whose cards are all just a picture, a title and at most a short note (ways to other
    pages) is a list of rows on phones: picture beside title, the note under it (DS-73, DS-116).
  - A card alone in its group takes the spare room: picture beside its text from 750 px (DS-74).
  A group of four or eight cards goes two, then four, across, so no card sits alone (DS-44).
  Any other count that would leave a short last row gives the spare room to its first cards
  (DS-52): five cards go two wider ones, then three, on wide screens; an odd count starts with one
  wide card, image beside text, where cards go two across.
  A group whose cards all have a logo (the three organisations on About Us) shows as rows, each
  logo beside its text (DS-50).
  A group without a heading has its card titles at H2, so no heading level is skipped after the
  page's H1. Each group can be linked to by its handle, e.g. /pages/donate#donate-ways-to-give, so a
  page's call to action can jump to it (DS-53).
  When the first group has no heading, the cards continue the text before them ("Current volunteer
  roles include the following:"), so they follow it at a group's space, not a section's (DS-58).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign groups = page.metafields.custom.card_groups.value -%}
{%- if groups != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign continues = false
    for group in groups limit: 1
      if group.heading.value == blank
        assign continues = true
      endif
    endfor
  -%}
  <div class="gs-section gs-surface-paper{% if continues %} gs-section--continues{% endif %}">
    <div class="gs-container">
      {%- for group in groups -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign heading = group.heading.value
          assign card_heading = 'h2'
          if heading != blank
            assign card_heading = 'h3'
          endif
          assign portrait = true
          assign logos = true
          assign docs = true
          assign offers = true
          assign links = true
          for card in group.cards.value
            assign ratio = card.image.value.aspect_ratio | default: 1
            assign card_link = card.link.value
            capture card_url
              render 'gs-url', link: card_link
            endcapture
            assign card_pdf = card_url | strip | split: '|' | last
            if ratio >= 1 or card_pdf == '1'
              assign portrait = false
            endif
            if card.logo.value == blank
              assign logos = false
            endif
            if card_pdf != '1'
              assign docs = false
            endif
            if card.image.value == blank or card_link.text == blank
              assign offers = false
            endif
            if card.image.value == blank or card_link.text != blank or card_link.url == blank or card_pdf == '1'
              assign links = false
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        <section class="gs-card-group" id="{{ group.system.handle }}"{% if heading != blank %} aria-labelledby="{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}"{% endif %}>
          {%- if heading != blank -%}
            <div class="gs-section-head">
              <h2 class="gs-h2" id="{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}">{{ heading | escape }}</h2>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign count = group.cards.value.size
            capture mods
              render 'gs-grid-modifiers', count: count
            endcapture
            assign mods = mods | strip_newlines
            assign fours = false
            if mods contains 'fours'
              assign fours = true
            endif
            if logos
              assign grid = 'gs-grid--logos'
            elsif docs
              assign grid = 'gs-grid--artworks'
            elsif portrait
              assign grid = 'gs-grid--people'
              if fours
                assign grid = grid | append: ' gs-grid--fours'
              endif
            elsif offers
              assign grid = 'gs-grid--cards gs-grid--rows'
            else
              assign grid = 'gs-grid--cards' | append: mods
            endif
            if links and logos == false and portrait == false and offers == false
              assign grid = grid | append: ' gs-grid--links'
            endif
          -%}
          <ul class="gs-grid {{ grid }}" role="list">
            {%- for card in group.cards.value -%}
              {%- liquid
                # The width each card's picture is shown at, so the browser fetches the right file.
                # Phones show one card across, or a link card's small picture beside its words.
                assign card_sizes = blank
                assign phone_sizes = '92vw'
                if links
                  assign phone_sizes = '37vw'
                endif
                if portrait and fours
                  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1296px) 276px, (min-width: 990px) 22vw, 46vw'
                elsif portrait
                  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1296px) 276px, (min-width: 990px) 22vw, (min-width: 750px) 30vw, 46vw'
                elsif offers
                  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1296px) 384px, (min-width: 750px) 31vw, 92vw'
                else
                  capture card_sizes
                    render 'gs-grid-sizes', mods: mods, index: forloop.index, phone: phone_sizes
                  endcapture
                  assign card_sizes = card_sizes | strip
                  if card_sizes == blank and links
                    assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1296px) 384px, (min-width: 990px) 31vw, (min-width: 750px) 47vw, 37vw'
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              {%- if docs -%}
                <li>{%- render 'gs-doc-tile', title: card.title.value, cover: card.image.value, url: card.link.value.url, text: card.text.value, heading: card_heading -%}</li>
              {%- else -%}
                <li>{%- render 'gs-card', card: card, heading: card_heading, portrait: portrait, sizes: card_sizes -%}</li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </section>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Card groups",
  "tag": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["page"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows the page's Card groups field. Cards with an image show as image cards, cards without one as text cards. Cards with a logo show the logo as their heading; a group of them shows as rows."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Card groups"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
